From f2fe21c89132f35cc7be1c1367b91044d4314420 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hung Fan Lin <leolin84200704@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 11:29:02 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] [VP-18480] Log one caller_attribution line per request (who
 called which route)

Phase A of the LIS-Sample -> trans merge needs a caller table per route
built from request logs, not from sampled spans or code search (a caller
configured only in Kubernetes is invisible to grep). This adds a structured
'caller_attribution' event emitted on response 'finish' by the existing
LoggerMiddleware: method, matched Express route pattern, path without
query string, status, latency, x-request-id, user-agent, x-forwarded-for,
remote ip, and a fixed allowlist of JWT claims (sub, client_id, user_id,
customer_id, internal_user_name, role) decoded without verification -- the
guards already verified the token; this is attribution, not authorisation.
No bodies, no query strings, no patient fields.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
